        "label": "C9",
        "rationale": "This candidate has direct mechanism evidence for JAK1 and JAK2 inhibition and human bioactivity showing median pChEMBL values of 8.23 across 26 JAK1 activities, 8.24 across 30 JAK2 activities, 7.28 across 13 TYK2 activities, and 8.09 across 9 AAK1 activities. TYK2 has a COVID-19 association score of 0.60374362. The packet therefore supports plausible engagement of COVID-19-associated signaling targets, but not whether this inhibition is beneficial in the disease.",
        "objection": "No supplied evidence demonstrates improved COVID-19 outcomes from this mechanism, so direction remains unresolved. The evidence also includes multiple Black Box Warnings and some off-target activity, including 7.53 across 2 STAT3 activities and 7.7 across 3 BMP2K activities, which adds uncertainty about interpretation and risk.",
